@startuml plan_mode_review_sequence
' Source baseline: pi-mono-java 09b32d8ea4a4b43b34be302d8b2745bdc417c9a2.
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeControlEventService.java :: accept.
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/persistence/MyBatisRuntimeExecutionControlRepository.java :: markConfirming, acceptConfirmation, claimConfirmation.
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/runtime/RuntimeSessionControlDispatcher.java :: dispatchConfirmation.
' Observed behavior: tool confirmation closes one response and resumes through a new fixed segment.
' Design reason: target-only plan review reuses this transport and durable handoff.
' Java divergence: immutable plan event identity is the approval target; tool permissions remain separate.
title CampusClaw Plan Review - Target Sequence
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 260
autonumber
actor User
participant "Runtime client" as UI
participant "POST Events\naccepting instance" as API
participant "Plan review service\nand persistence" as Service
database GaussDB as DB
participant "Control dispatcher\noriginal instance" as Dispatcher
participant "Original execution\nExitPlanMode / Agent" as Agent

group Plan mode is active; an ordinary message already started this execution
  Agent -> Agent : Produce one ExitPlanMode call with complete Markdown
  Agent -> Service : Persist unique tool_call; beginReview(fixed target, call, plan)
  Service -> DB : Lock Session and execution; validate active plan mode
  Service -> DB : Append agent.plan + confirming idle;
  note right of DB
    Same transaction records the internal pending plan
    and closes the current segment.
    Session remains running.
  end note
  DB --> Service : Commit
  Service --> UI : Original SSE: plan, confirming idle; close
  Agent -> Agent : Await plan decision; keep tools and current prompt
end

User -> UI : Approve or request revision
UI -> API : POST user.plan_confirmation(targetEventId, result)
API -> API : Reserve response / result wait capacity
API -> Service : Accept decision
Service -> DB : Lock Session and execution;
note right of DB
  Require the exact pending plan in this Session.
  Recheck root, branch, current segment and stop state.
end note
Service -> DB : Append confirmation; create continuation segment;
note right of DB
  Approve: update mode=build and append mode event.
  Revise: keep mode=plan and persist feedback.
  Clear pending plan. Keep Session running.
end note
DB --> Service : Commit fixed continuation target
Service --> API : Accepted confirmation
API --> UI : First SSE frame: full committed confirmation
API -> Dispatcher : Local notify if original execution is local
note over DB,Dispatcher
  Existing database control polling is the fallback.
  The accepting instance does not reconstruct credentials.
end note
Dispatcher -> DB : Claim decision with fixed original target
DB --> Dispatcher : Committed decision, once
Dispatcher -> Agent : Bind new segment output; complete pending Future
alt Approved
  Agent -> Agent : Apply committed build mode to own system prompt
  Agent -> Service : Persist ExitPlanMode result approved=true
  Agent -> Agent : Next model request may implement the plan
else Revision requested
  Agent -> Service : Persist normal result approved=false and feedback
  Agent -> Agent : Next request keeps planning; a new plan gets a new eventId
end
Service --> UI : New SSE: committed mode/result/output via local or DB path
note over UI,Agent
  Every agent event keeps the original message sourceEventId.
  A new confirming or actual terminal idle closes this response.
  Disconnect closes observation only; it never grants approval.
end note
@enduml

@startuml plan_mode_state
' Source baseline: pi-mono-java 09b32d8ea4a4b43b34be302d8b2745bdc417c9a2.
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/session/RuntimeSessionState.java :: IDLE, RUNNING.
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeExecutionCoordinator.java :: timeout, commitAndRelease.
' Source: frontend/src/runtime/eventStore.ts :: executionState; the plan projection is target-only.
' Observed behavior: confirming closes HTTP output without releasing Session admission.
' Design reason: review stays in execution state; clients recover from events, without a Session pointer.
' Java divergence: manual mode switching is idle-only; approval exits within the original execution.
title CampusClaw Plan Mode - Target State and Admission
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam stateBackgroundColor #EFF6FF
skinparam stateBorderColor #64748B
hide empty description

state "Idle / Build\nstate=idle, mode=build" as Normal
state "Idle / Planning\nstate=idle, mode=plan" as PlanIdle
state "Exploring or designing\nstate=running, mode=plan" as Planning
state "Awaiting plan review\nstate=running, mode=plan\nExecution: CONFIRMING (internal)" as Reviewing
state "Implementing\nstate=running, mode=build" as Implementing

[*] --> Normal : create
Normal --> PlanIdle : POST Session mode=plan + valid ETag
PlanIdle --> Normal : POST Session mode=build + valid ETag
PlanIdle --> Planning : accept user.message
Planning --> PlanIdle : ordinary question / answer ends execution
Planning --> Reviewing : ExitPlanMode; commit plan and confirming idle
Reviewing --> Planning : accept revise; resume with feedback
Reviewing --> Implementing : accept approve; resume next step
Normal --> Implementing : accept user.message
Implementing --> Normal : actual terminal committed
Planning --> PlanIdle : actual stop / failure committed
Reviewing --> PlanIdle : actual stop / failure committed

note bottom of Reviewing
  A closed SSE is not an execution terminal.
  New messages and Session mode updates are rejected.
  Only the current plan event can be confirmed.
  Existing tool permission review is independent.
end note
@enduml


