title CampusClaw TodoUpdate - Target Tool and Event Flow
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 210
autonumber
participant "AgentLoop / Pipeline" as Loop
participant "TodoUpdateTool\n(target-only)" as Todo
participant "RuntimeEventProjector" as Projector
database "Existing entries / events" as DB
participant "Client event store\n+ deriveTodos (target-only)" as UI
participant "Existing history API" as History

Loop -> Projector : Finalized TodoUpdate call (complete list)
Projector -> DB : Commit generic tool_call
Projector --> UI : agent.tool_call
note right of UI
  Show updating if useful.
  Do not replace committed progress yet.
end note
Loop -> Todo : Validate schema; execute(args)
alt Valid complete list
  Todo --> Loop : AgentToolResult with one JSON text block
  Loop -> Projector : Existing TurnEndEvent with tool results
  Projector -> Projector : Encode and check complete frame size
  Projector -> DB : Commit ToolResult Entry and public event
  DB --> Projector : Committed
  Projector --> UI : agent.tool_result (isError=false)
  UI -> UI : Match sourceEventId + toolCallId;
  note right of UI
    Check call.toolName and result JSON.
    Replace the complete TODO projection.
  end note
else Invalid or failed
  Todo --> Loop : Existing tool error path
  Loop -> Projector : Existing TurnEndEvent with failed result
  Projector -> DB : Commit failed generic result
  Projector --> UI : agent.tool_result (isError=true)
  UI -> UI : Keep previous successful list
end
note over Loop,UI
  Ordinary thinking, messages and business tools continue.
  No confirmation idle, new segment, mode update or TODO endpoint.
  Each later update replaces the list; actual execution terminal stays independent.
end note
UI -> History : GET Events
History -> DB : Read stored generic calls and results
DB --> History : Ordered stored events
History --> UI : Existing history response
UI -> UI : Reconcile events and run the same projection
@enduml
